Either of these two problems unfolds into a challenge due to the unknown variables that need to be estimated, such as the communication distance, the impact of the geometry of the emitters and receivers, or the fluid velocity in vessel-like media.
Due to the difficulty of these problems, literature reports {NN}-based solutions leveraging on their capacity as universal approximators.
{NNs} can be used either to estimate the parameters for a given model or as a model-independent method to estimate the {CIR}.
In the following subsections, we detail various {MC} scenarios and the reported {NN}-based estimators.

