\subsubsection{Concluding Remarks}

The use of {NNs} for {MC} channel estimation has mostly focused on feedforward {NN} and \ac{CNN} architectures.
Feedforward {NNs} are used to estimate specific parameters in the channel, and \ac{CNN} architectures are adopted for the more ambitious goal of estimating the {CIR}.
This subject still requires further development of {NNs} to target more realistic scenarios.
Particularly in {IoBNT} contexts, both short-range channels, such as cell-to-cell, and long-range channels, like those through the human circulatory system, are lacking from modeling with {NNs}.

