\section{Enabling Biocomputing in IoBNT Networks}
\label{sec_bio_AI}

One particular challenge in nanoscale computing is the development of biocompatible nanoprocessing nodes.\footnote{Although this is a hardware-like requisite, much focus is also on new theoretical developments of computability, see \cite{goimoreno2024biocomputation,dehghani2024bioinspired}.}
Nanonodes are projected to perform the needed computation and host smart processing modules with biocompatible premises, as needed in {IoBNT} networks; see \cite{marzo2019nanonetworks}.
Bio-inspired micro/nano computer design is a relatively young research field; therefore, the literature reflects varying readiness levels of individual concepts, which we summarize in this section.
Developments in this area lay the foundation to support the intelligent capabilities of the nanocomponents of the {IoBNT} networks.
This section summarizes the most recent trends in technological development and identifies one of the most promising research areas for further advancements.

