\subsection{Biocomputing in the Digital Domain}

Logic gates and registers are the constituent elements to perform arithmetic operations in the digital domain; see \cite[Sec. 5.2.1]{brown2009fundamentals}.
The adders and multiplier blocks needed to implement {NNs} can be digitally implemented as a combination of \texttt{AND}, \texttt{OR}, and \texttt{XOR} gates.
Following this thought, we describe the early developments of logic and \ac{DSP} operations in the digital domain in the following sections.

