\subsubsection{Logic gates and {NNs} with \acp{CRN}}

The first description of \acp{CRN} realizing neuron components of {NNs} dates to the work in \cite{hjelmfelt1991chemical}, where a neuron was prototyped through an enzyme reaction system.\footnote{\ac{CRN} is an abstraction of the dynamics of a system of chemical reactions given by a finite set of differential equations; see \cite[Sec. 3.1]{nagipogu2023survey}.}
Subsequent work develops neurons through the connection of logic gates, where a \num{2}-neuron feedforward {NN} is realized in \cite{agiza2024phcontrolled} to perform as a classifier of black and white images.
The linear neuron operation, as shown in appendix, \Cref{fig_NN_architecture}, results from mixing encoded bit-1s and bit-0s, analogous to acid and base compounds.
The non-linear component of the neuron is realized by thresholding with the pH indicator.
The classifier identifies $8\times 8 $ resolution images of handwritten digits with an accuracy larger than $\SI{95}{\percent}$.\footnote{The handwritten images are taken from the \ac{MNIST} database \cite{deng2012mnist}.}

