\subsection{{NN}'s Hyperparameters}
\label{boxTech_hyper}

Hyperparameters refer to those components of the {NN} whose numerical values can not be derived from the dataset, as they define the architecture per se.
Consequently, they are not part of the training process \cite{yang2020hyperparameter}.
These are components related to
%
\begin{itemize}
    \item the architecture, such as the number of nodes and hidden layers, drop-out rate,
    %
    \item the selection of the loss function type, such as binary cross-entropy, multiclass cross-entropy, \acf{RMSprop},
    %
    \item the selection of the activation functions, such as sigmoid, \acf{ReLU}, 'softmax', 'tanh', 'softsign',
    %
    \item the training parameters such as the batch size \cite{agrawal2021hyperparameter}, learning rate \cite{jin2000improvements}, momentum \cite{rumelhart1987learning}, number of epochs), or
    %
    \item the selection of the optimizer, such as \ac{SGD}, Adam, \ac{RMSprop}. 
\end{itemize}
%
These are parameters set by experience and by validating the operation of the {NN}.
\newline
A rule of thumb to manually set these parameters is to tune them during the training and validation phases; see \cite[Sec. 5.3]{oshea2017introduction}.
The dataset can be divided into \SI{80}{\percent} for training, \SI{10}{\percent} for validation, and \SI{10}{\percent} for testing.
The {NN} is trained with the given set of hyperparameters and adjusted till verifying performance within the validation test.
If good performance is also obtained within the testing set, then this is a good candidate for the {NN} hyperparameters.

The hyperparameters can also be automatically tuned, and various tuning methods exist in the literature.
Examples of implemented algorithms include the grid search (a brute-force approach) and random search (a less computationally costly approach).
More elaborate algorithms, such as the popular \ac{SGD} or Bayesian optimization, exploit the impact of hyperparameter variability on {NN} performance; see further details in \cite{yang2020hyperparameter}.

