Given $T \in \B(\ell^2(X))$, we have $T \in \CC^*_{\dyn,\q}(\G)$ \emph{if and only if} there exists $T_n \in \B(\ell^2(X_n))$ for each $n\in \N$ with $\sup_{n\in \N} \|T_n\| < \infty$ such that $T = (\SOT)-\sum_{n \in \N} T_n$ and for any $\epsilon > 0$ there exists $L>0$ satisfying: for any $n\in \N$ and $A_n,B_n \subseteq X_n$ with $d_n(A_n, B_n) > L$, we have $\|\chi_{A_n} T_n\chi_{B_n}\| < \epsilon$. A similar result holds for $\CC^*_{\dyn}(\G)$.
