\section{Conclusion}\label{sec:conclu}
This work investigates the stochastic precoding design by using the first and second moments of fading channels. As compared to the existing works that assume a particular channel distribution, our method has the advantage of working for a generic fading model; as compared to the existing works that adopt a model-free approach, our method has the advantage of providing more efficient optimization. The heart of our method lies in a stochastic extension of the existing matrix FP methods. Although this paper focuses on the downlink network, the proposed algorithm can be readily adapted to other network topologies such as device-to-device, uplink, and cell-free.
