Instead of a detailed analysis as in the dimerized case, we now only focus on the main features of
the entropy spreading during domain-wall melting. It is easy to guess that, to leading order, the half-chain entropy should now be given by
%
\eq{
S = \frac{1}{2} \ln t + \mathrm{const},
\label{Strim}}
%
which is just three times the $\delta=0$ result \eqref{Sdw}, reflecting the contributions from
three completely filled bands. As shown in Fig. \ref{fig:enthalftrim}, the numerical results agree
very well with the ansatz \eqref{Strim}, up to oscillations decaying with time.

