\begin{abstract}
In this article, we study a double phase variable exponent Kirchhoff problem. We employ a well-known critical point result by Bonanno and Chinn\`{\i} and show the existence of at least three solutions. We introduce a novel $n$-dimensional vector inequality, Proposition \ref{Prop:2.2}, which is a crucial auxiliary result to obtain the $C^{1}-$regularity of the energy functional.
\end{abstract}

\begin{keywords}
Double phase variable exponent problem; $p(x)$-Kirchhoff problem; critical point theory; Musielak-Orlicz Sobolev space
\end{keywords}

