Through the above two simulation studies, it has been demonstrated that the proposed methods LFR and LFR$^k$ can accurately estimate regression curves even when the response variables lie on a manifold, where conventional regression methods for real-valued responses are not directly applicable. 
Moreover, by using LFR$^k$, it becomes unnecessary to compute geodesic distances on the manifold, resulting in a substantial reduction in computational cost.
