We jointly constrain cosmological and FRB-related DM parameters, and adopt flat priors for the following seven parameters: 
$\Omega_{\rm m} \in \mathcal{U}(0.28, 0.35)$ \citep{Yang:2022ftm}, 
$\Omega_{\rm b} \in \mathcal{U}(0.01, 0.10)$, 
$H_{0} \in \mathcal{U}(20, 140)~\rm km\ s^{-1}\ Mpc^{-1}$, 
$f_{\rm d} \in \mathcal{U}(0.84, 0.96)$,\footnote{This prior on $f_{\rm d}$ is informed by observations of the baryon fraction in stars ($f_*$) and cold gas ($f_{\rm cold}$), independent of FRBs. Assuming a conservative flat prior for $f_*$ extended by a factor of five, the diffuse baryon fraction is inferred via $f_{\rm d} = 1 - f_* - f_{\rm cold}$ \citep{connor2025gas}.} 
$F \in \mathcal{U}(0.011, 1.0)$, 
$\mu_{\rm host} \in \mathcal{U}(3.0, 5.3)$, 
and $\sigma_{\rm host} \in \mathcal{U}(0.2, 2.0)$ \citep{Macquart:2020lln}.
The GW population model parameters include $\alpha$, $\beta$, $m_{\rm min}$, $m_{\rm max}$, $\Delta m$, $\mu_{\rm g}$, $\sigma_{\rm g}$, $\lambda_{\rm peak}$, $\gamma$, $\kappa$, and $z_{\rm p}$, which are fixed to the inferred values of \citet{LIGOScientific:2021aug}.
