We utilize the {\tt bilby}\footnote{\url{https://github.com/bilby-dev/bilby}} package to perform Markov Chain Monto Carlo (MCMC) analysis and choose the {\tt emcee}\footnote{\url{https://emcee.readthedocs.io/en/stable}} sampler. We use the {\tt ICAROGW}\footnote{\url{https://github.com/simone-mastrogiovanni/icarogw}} package to do the hierarchic Bayesian analysis of GW standard sirens, and the {\tt GetDist}\footnote{\url{https://github.com/cmbant/getdist}} package to plot the marginalized posterior distributions. The final likelihood $\mathcal{L}$ used in our analysis is the combination of $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FRB}}$ and $\mathcal{L}_{\rm GW}$ in Eqs.~(\ref{eq:FRB likelihood}) and~(\ref{eq:GW likelihood}), respectively, which is written as 
\begin{equation}
\ln \mathcal{L}=\ln \left(\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FRB}}\right)+\ln \left(\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{GW}}\right).
\label{Eq:Eq11}
\end{equation}


