If $\widetilde{\Gamma}$ has finite abelianization, then there exists a character $\chi \in \widehat{\mathbb Z}$ such that
$\chi \circ c \in Z^2(\Gamma, \mathbb{T})$ is not a coboundary.
\end{proposition}

