      \field{labelnamesource}{author}
      \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
      \field{abstract}{We study the twisted Ruelle zeta function {\$}{\$}{\backslash}zeta {\_}X(s){\$}{\$} for smooth Anosov vector fields X acting on flat vector bundles over smooth compact manifolds. In dimension 3, we prove the Fried conjecture, relating Reidemeister torsion and {\$}{\$}{\backslash}zeta {\_}X(0){\$}{\$}. In higher dimensions, we show more generally that {\$}{\$}{\backslash}zeta {\_}X(0){\$}{\$} is locally constant with respect to the vector field X under a spectral condition. As a consequence, we also show the Fried conjecture for Anosov flows near the geodesic flow on the unit tangent bundle of hyperbolic 3-manifolds. This gives the first examples of non-analytic Anosov flows and geodesic flows in variable negative curvature where the Fried conjecture holds true.}
