      \field{abstract}{LetX be a compact complex manifold covered by complex hyperbolicn-space with the induced metric. Each stable horocycle has a cocomplex structure preserved by the geodesic flow. To a closed geodesic $\gamma$ one can thus associate a piece of the Poincaré map with a holomorphic fixed point. The resulting Atiyah-Bott fixed point indices, together with the length and multiplicity of $\gamma$ as a periodic orbit, determine the contribution of $\gamma$ to certain zeta functionsRp(z), 0≦p≦n. From the leading coefficient ofRpatZ=0 and the Hodge numbershij(X) we calculate the Ray-Singer{\$}{\$}{\backslash}bar {\backslash}partial {\$}{\$}-torsionTp(X). This indicates that the known connections between torsion and the dynamical features of closed orbits continue to hold in the holomorphic category.}
