\subsection{Model Training}
To ensure an effective evaluation and comparison with previous studies, the target datasets were divided into two parts every time. After preparing the feature set, we perform the data normalization and split the feature data into 80\% training data and 20\% testing data . The model was trained on the Augmented dataset using 500 epochs. To tune the hyperparameter, we used a learning rate of 0.0001, batch size 256, optimizer ‘Adam’ with loss function categorical- crossentropy. The whole process is developed using TensorFlow and Keras to build and train a deep learning model for our SER framework. Experiments were conducted using CPU(11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1165G7 @ 2.80GHz 2.80 GHz) and RAM (16GB); training each fold took approximately 7 hours.

