\section{Conclusions}
Since sQRy are primarily conceived for user interaction, 
most of the available payload within them is typically used for text strings. 
The compression method presented in a preliminary form in this work and its integration within sQRy permits to reduce occupancy sensibly. 
In the example related to Wi-Fi equipment presented here, the compressed sQRy has an occupancy of $91.4\%$ compared to the uncompressed case.

The proposed method is just the first step in the research for code compression techniques, and conceiving
better strategies is part of our planned future work.
We will focus on those approaches that do not require any additional changes concerning the way they are incorporated into the sQRy and, consequently, the apps that implement the execution chain. 




