admitted a unique strong solution. Moreover, the fact that $\Qp$ and $\Pp$ share the same null set ensures that $(L,U)\in\cD$ under $\Qp$. In other words, $(L,U)$ is also adapted in accordance with ambiguity. For brevity, we write $X^{0,L,U}=X^A $.
