    \label{im:EP4_Kr2i_var}
\end{figure}

Competitive binding also plays an important role for cAMP expression since the inhibiting G-protein $G_{\alpha_i}$ prevents binding of AC to the stimulating G-protein $G_{\alpha_s}$. In  model~\eqref{eq:EP4full} competitive binding of $G_{\alpha_s}$ and $G_{\alpha_i}$ to AC  is  determined by the parameter $K_{ai}$. 
Varying the dissociation constant $K_{ai}$ for AC6 and G$_{\alpha_i}$  only affects cAMP levels but does not change the qualitative cAMP dynamics nor the gradual increase of cAMP  with respect to PGE2, see Figure~\ref{im:EP4_Kai_var} in Appendix.




